.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 26, 2026
.Dt LOGIN.CONF 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm login.conf
.Nd login class capability database
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The file
.Pa /etc/login.conf
describes login classes: the resource limits, environment and other
settings a session starts with.
An account's class is the fifth field of
.Pa /etc/master.passwd ;
see
.Xr passwd 5 .
An empty class means
.Dq default ,
except that the superuser's means
.Dq root .
A class with no record uses
.Dq default .
.Pp
Like
.Xr gettytab 5 ,
it is a
.Xr getcap 3
database, and
.Cm tc Ns = Ns Ar class
continues a record with another class.
Sizes take the suffixes
.Cm b ,
.Cm k ,
.Cm m ,
.Cm g
and
.Cm t ;
times take
.Cm s ,
.Cm m ,
.Cm h ,
.Cm d
and
.Cm w ,
and may be combined, as in
.Ql 1h30m .
Either may be
.Ql unlimited .
.Ss Resource limits
Each limit sets both the soft and hard limit;
.Ar name Ns Cm -cur
and
.Ar name Ns Cm -max
set one of them.
.Bl -column "coredumpsize" "size"
.It Sy Name Ta Sy Type Ta Sy Limit
.It coredumpsize Ta size Ta Dv RLIMIT_CORE
.It cputime Ta time Ta Dv RLIMIT_CPU
.It datasize Ta size Ta Dv RLIMIT_DATA
.It filesize Ta size Ta Dv RLIMIT_FSIZE
.It maxproc Ta number Ta Dv RLIMIT_NPROC
.It memorylocked Ta size Ta Dv RLIMIT_MEMLOCK
.It memoryuse Ta size Ta Dv RLIMIT_RSS
.It openfiles Ta number Ta Dv RLIMIT_NOFILE
.It stacksize Ta size Ta Dv RLIMIT_STACK
.El
.Ss Environment and session
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm charset Ns = Ns Ar name
.Ev MM_CHARSET .
.It Cm hushlogin
Do not print the message of the day.
.It Cm lang Ns = Ns Ar locale
.Ev LANG .
.It Cm nologin Ns = Ns Ar file
Refuse logins other than the superuser's while
.Ar file
exists, showing its contents.
.It Cm path Ns = Ns Ar directories
.Ev PATH ,
as a space-separated list.
.It Cm priority Ns = Ns Ar number
The scheduling priority, as for
.Xr nice 1 .
.It Cm requirehome
Refuse the login if the home directory is missing.
.It Cm setenv Ns = Ns Ar list
Further variables, as
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
pairs separated by commas;
.Ql \e,
is a literal comma.
In each value,
.Ql ~
stands for the home directory and
.Ql $
for the user name.
.It Cm shell Ns = Ns Ar program
Run
.Ar program
instead of the account's shell.
.It Cm timezone Ns = Ns Ar zone
.Ev TZ .
.It Cm umask Ns = Ns Ar mask
The file creation mask, in octal.
.It Cm welcome Ns = Ns Ar file
The message of the day; default
.Pa /etc/motd .
.El
.Ss Authentication
These are read from the
.Dq default
class only.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm login-backoff Ns = Ns Ar number
Failed attempts after which
.Xr login 1
starts delaying; default 3.
.It Cm login-retries Ns = Ns Ar number
Failed attempts after which it gives up; default 10.
.It Cm login-timeout Ns = Ns Ar seconds
How long a login may take; default 300.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/login.conf -compact
.It Pa /etc/login.conf
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr login 1 ,
.Xr getcap 3 ,
.Xr getrlimit 2 ,
.Xr passwd 5
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
file appeared in
.Bsx 2.1 .
.Cm login-timeout
is OxideBSD's.
